{
  "title": "Tibial Eminence Fracture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4022/tibial-eminence-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 1 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A Tibial Eminence Fracture, also known as a tibial spine fracture, is an intra-articular fracture of the bony attachment of the ACL on the tibia that is most commonly seen in children from age 8 to 14 years during athletic activity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be confirmed with radiographs of the knee. MRI studies can be helpful for determining associated ligamentous/meniscal damage.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is closed reduction and casting or open reduction and fixation depending on the degree of displacement and success of closed reduction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "2-5% of knee injuries with effusion in the pediatric population",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in **ages 8-14**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "traumatic mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rapid deceleration or hyperextension/rotation of the knee, as in sports",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "same mechanism that would cause **ACL tear in adult**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fall from bike or motorcycle (typically resulting in hyperextension)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occur in **40% of eminence fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "meniscal injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "collateral ligament injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "capsular damage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "osteochondral fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tibial eminence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**non-articular** portion of the tibia between the medial and lateral tibial plateau",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/tibial%20eminence.jpg",
                      "caption": "tibial eminence anatomy"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Consists of two spines: ACL attaches to medial spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ACL insertion is 9mm posterior to the intermeniscal ligament and adjacent to anterior horns of meniscus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "PCL does not attach to tibia spines",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Pediatric specific",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Intercondylar eminence in incompletely ossified and is more prone to failure than ligamentous structures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Failure occurs through deep cancellous bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Fracture usually confined to intercondylar eminence, but it may propagate to tibial plateau, medial is most common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior cruciate ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inserts 10-14 mm behind anterior border of tibia and extends to medial and lateral tibial eminence",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Modified Meyers and McKeever Classification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nondisplaced (<3mm)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/tibial%20eminence%20classification.jpg",
                          "caption": "Type 1 illustration"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/nondisplaced%20tibial%20eminence.jpg",
                          "caption": "Type I MRI"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Minimally displaced with intact posterior hinge",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/tibial%20eminence%20classification%202.jpg",
                          "caption": "Type II illustration"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/type%202.jpg",
                          "caption": "Type II radiograph"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Completely displaced",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/tibial%20eminence%20classification%203.jpg",
                          "caption": "Type III illustration"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/type%20iii.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III+",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III fracture with rotation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type IV",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Completely displaced, rotated, comminuted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/meyers%20mckeever.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "severe swelling and pain in the knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inability to bear weight",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**immediate knee effusion due to hemarthrosis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Knee usually in flexed position**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ROM",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often limited secondary to pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "once pain is controlled, lack of motion may indicate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "meniscal pathology",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "displaced/entrapped fracture fragment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "positive anterior drawer",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most useful for determining fracture displacement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "intercondylar",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "oblique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "helpful in determining the extent of tibial plateau involvement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "useful for pre-operative planning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "used when fracture displacement cannot be determined by plain radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "better at determining associated ligamentous/meniscal damage than CT or radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Majority of fractures show no additional internal derangement (meniscus injuries)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "15-37% of cases have associated intra-articular pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction, aspiration of hemarthrosis, immobilization in full extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "non-displaced type I and reducible type II fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduction technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "see techniques below",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "immobilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "cast in extension for 3-4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "patients get extremely stiff with prolonged immobilization",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "allows for gradual rehab program",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ORIF vs. all-arthroscopic fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III or Type II fractures that cannot be reduced",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "type II fractures may fail to reduce due to the **entrapped medial meniscus**, entrapped intermeniscal ligament, or the pull of the lateral meniscus attachment",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "block to extension",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed Reduction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "aspiration",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "when tense hemarthrosis is present, needle aspiration with the injection of lidocaine may help extend the knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extend the knee to full extension or hyperextension to observe for fragment reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cast is placed at 0 degrees of flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cast in extension for 3-4 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "confirmation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral radiograph to confirm reduction, and then serial radiographs to observe maintenance of reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "CT or MRI may be used when the adequacy of reduction is unclear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Arthroscopic fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "standard arthroscopic portals",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "debride fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "disengage **entrapped meniscus or intermeniscal ligament**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "medial meniscus entrapment most common",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "reduce fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "fracture fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**suture fixation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Large avulsed fragments may be repaired directly",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Smaller avulsed fragments (usually in an older patient) may require sutures through the base of the ACL",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "pros",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "minimal damage to physis",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "growth at level of physis will disrupt non-absorbable sutures to allow for continued growth",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "cons",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "technically demanding",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**screw fixation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4022/images/screw%20fixation.jpg",
                          "caption": "fixation with screw"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "pros",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "less demanding than suture fixation",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "possibly earlier mobilization",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "cons",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "requires larger osteochondral fragment",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "hardware irritation",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "not possible for small, comminuted fragments",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "impingement from an improperly placed screw",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "risk of iatrogenic comminution",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**requires removal only if malpositioned**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "physeal damage",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**post-operative care**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "immobilize with cast in extension for 7-10 days and repeat radiographs to ensure no displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "This is variable, some surgeon allow immediate ROM",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "early controlled range of motion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "length of limited weight bearing is controversial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Open fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "same principles as arthroscopic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Loss of motion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "very common, especially loss of extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be due to displaced fragment impinging on femoral notch",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Arthrofibrosis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**more common with surgical reconstruction**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "concomitant ACL injury is an independent risk factor for the need to return to the OR for MUA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Growth arrest**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "from iatrogenic injury during surgery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**ACL laxity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "38-100%, more common in operatively treated knees",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Lachman's laxity may be noted compared to contralateral limb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "functional instability is uncommon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Rate of ACL reconstruction following this injury is 15-25%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Overall prognosis is good with 85% returning to prior level of sport**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
